   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the town of Austerlitz, in the county of Columbia, to discontinue the use of certain lands as parklands",
    "basePrintNo": "S5735",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5735-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Columbia County",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5735\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to authorize the town of Austerlitz, in the county of Columbia,\nto discontinue the use of certain lands as parklands\n\n PURPOSE :\nTo allow the town of Austerlitz to alienate and dedicate parkland to\npermit the construction of a new firehouse for the Austerlitz\nVolunteer Fire Company.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 authorizes the town of Austerlitz, through its town board,\nto discontinue designated parkland and in exchange dedicate other\nlands as parkland.\n\nSection 2 authorizes the discontinuation of certain parkland only upon\nthe condition of the town dedicating additional parkland of equal or\ngreater value.\n\nSection 3 describes the lands authorized to be discontinued as\nparkland.\n\nSection 4 describes the replacement lands to be dedicated by the town\nof Austerlitz.\n\nSection 5 requires the town of Austerlitz to dedicate the difference\nof the fair market value of the lands alienated if the lands dedicated\nare not equal or greater in value than the parkland discontinued.\n\nSection 6 authorizes the discontinuation and conveyance of parkland\nonly when the town of Austerlitz has complied with federal\nrequirements.\n\nSection 7 sets an immediate effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nIn 1979, the town of Austerlitz purchased approximately 4.39 acres of\nvacant land to be used for park and recreational purposes. That parcel\nsurrounds on three sides, a 0.63 acre parcel owned by the Austerlitz\nFire District No.1. The firehouse on this parcel is seriously\ndeteriorated and is insufficient to adequately serve the Volunteer\nFire Company. In order to replace the current firehouse with a modem,\nsufficiently sized firehouse, more acreage is necessary for the\nbuilding.\n\nTo help alleviate the problem, the Town proposed a land swap with the\nFire District. The Town proposes transferring a 1.88 acre parcel to\nthe Fire District and in exchange receive a 3.00 acre parcel from 49\nEast Houston Street Corporation, to provide a continuous 5.48 parcel\nto be used for park and recreation purposes.\n\nSurveys and appraisals have been completed on the affected parcels.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
